From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Salah Ahmed <haddad2inc@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 05 Oct 2026 02:32:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spi-nor: macronix: restore MX25L12805D name

The backport of the upstream fix for this part (d9f8ecc394,
439-v7.4-mtd-spi-nor-macronix-Restore-fallback-parameters-for.patch,
upstream 01739ccea21b) restored the static .size and .no_sfdp_flags of
the SNOR_ID(0xc2, 0x20, 0x18) entry, but not its .name.

Without .name, spi_nor_sysfs_is_visible() returns 0 for partname, so the
attribute is not exposed at all and a running board cannot report which
name the driver matched. Restore that one field, as the neighbouring
mx25l3205d and mx25l6405d entries still carry theirs, keeping the same
".id then .name" order they use.

This labels the table entry, not the die: any part reporting JEDEC id
c22018 shows partname=mx25l12805d, so partname alone cannot tell them
apart. The sfdp blob can, and its absence is itself the answer for the
part this patch is about - 01739ccea21b records that the legacy
MX25L12805D "lacks SFDP support entirely", while the newer MX25L12833F
shares the same id and does support SFDP. On such a board sfdp is not
exposed either, so partname is the only positive label it gets.

Data-only: probing is unchanged, since JEDEC detection still overrides
a name match for entries with an id, and spi_nor_scan() falls back to
dev_name(dev) for mtd->name, so mtd device names and partitions are
unaffected.

Tested on a COMFAST CF-WA350 (QCA9563, 16 MiB Macronix, jedec_id c22018,
Linux 6.18.54, GCC 14.4.0): /sys/bus/spi/devices/spi0.0/spi-nor/ exposes
partname=mx25l12805d, manufacturer=macronix and jedec_id=c22018, and no
sfdp attribute. The board boots and the mtd layout is intact (u-boot,
art, firmware, kernel, rootfs, rootfs_data, art-backup).

Fixes: 947c86e481a0 ("mtd: spi-nor: macronix: Drop the redundant flash info fields")
Signed-off-by: Salah Ahmed <haddad2inc@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/mtd/spi-nor/macronix.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/macronix.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/macronix.c
@@ -143,6 +143,7 @@ static const struct flash_info macronix_
 	}, {
 		/* MX25L12805D */
 		.id = SNOR_ID(0xc2, 0x20, 0x18),
+		.name = "mx25l12805d",
 		.size = SZ_16M,
 		.flags = SPI_NOR_HAS_LOCK | SPI_NOR_4BIT_BP,
 		.no_sfdp_flags = SECT_4K,
